options.explanation:
$\begin{align}
\dfrac{d^2y}{dx^2}&=\dfrac{d}{dx}\left(-\dfrac{3x^2}{2y}\right)
\\\\
&=-\dfrac{d}{dx}\left(\dfrac{3x^2}{2y}\right)
\\\\
&=-\dfrac{\dfrac{d}{dx}(3x^2)\cdot 2y-3x^2\cdot\dfrac{d}{dx}(2y)}{4y^2}
\\\\
&=-\dfrac{3\cdot2x\cdot 2y-3x^2\cdot2\cdot\dfrac{dy}{dx}}{4y^2}
\\\\
&=-\dfrac{6xy-3x^2\cdot\dfrac{dy}{dx}}{2y^2}
\\\\
&=\dfrac{-6xy+3x^2\cdot\dfrac{dy}{dx}}{2y^2}
\end{align}$

Now let's plug $\goldD{\dfrac{dy}{dx}=-\dfrac{3x^2}{2y}}$ into the expression we got:

$\begin{align}
\dfrac{d^2y}{dx^2}&=\dfrac{-6xy+3x^2\cdot\goldD{\dfrac{dy}{dx}}}{2y^2}
\\\\
&=\dfrac{-6xy+3x^2\cdot\left(\goldD{-\dfrac{3x^2}{2y}}\right)}{2y^2}
\\\\
&=-\dfrac{12xy^2+9x^4}{4y^3}
\end{align}$

hints.content:
Finally, let's plug $\blueD{x=2}$ and $\maroonD{y=4}$ into the expression we got:

$\begin{align}
\left.-\dfrac{12\blueD x\maroonD y^2+9\blueD x^4}{4\maroonD y^3}\right\rvert_{(\blueD{2},\maroonD{4})}&=-\dfrac{12(\blueD{2})(\maroonD{4})^2+9(\blueD{2})^4}{4(\maroonD{4})^3}
\\\\
&=-\dfrac{33}{16}
\end{align}$
